[49m[38;5;10m+     1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # ERRORS.md — error / rejection surface table (Phase A, gates Phase C)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Mechanically derived from `c_src/src/driver.c`. The library is `void`-only: it
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m has **no return codes, no error enums, no `errno` use, no `assert`, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `return -1` / `return NULL`**. Every rejection is expressed as *a branch that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m prints a fixed diagnostic line instead of doing the work*, plus one silent
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m null-pointer guard. The complete set of conditionals in the C source is:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m src/driver.c:31   if (line != NULL)                     -> printLine null guard
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m src/driver.c:46   if (data >= 0) ... else               -> bad(): negative reject
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m src/driver.c:65   if (data >= 0) ... else               -> goodG2B(): dead branch (data == 7)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m src/driver.c:83   if (data >= 0 && data < (10)) ... else -> goodB2G(): range reject
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Constants that act as limits: `10` (both the `int buffer[10]` extent and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `goodB2G`'s upper bound). `bad()` has **no** upper bound — that omission is the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m injected defect and is row 8/9 below.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Observable result == exact stdout byte stream (and exit status).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | function | trigger (exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------|------------------------------------------|-------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1 | `printLine` | `line == NULL` | silent: returns without emitting a single byte |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 2 | `printIntLine` | *(none — no validation at all; every `int` incl. `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` is accepted)* | prints `"%d\n"` of the value |
