[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Harness pitfall worth recording
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `cargo test` does **not** build a `crate-type = ["cdylib"]` library: an
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m integration test cannot link against a cdylib, so Cargo has no reason to produce
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m it. A differential test that simply picks up `target/<profile>/libdriver.so`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m therefore verifies whatever `.so` was left behind by an earlier `cargo build` —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m edits to `src/lib.rs` are invisible and every run passes vacuously. This was
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m observed here: five deliberately injected bugs all "passed" until it was fixed.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `tests/common/mod.rs::rust_lib()` now (a) shells out to `cargo build --lib` with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the current profile and feature flags before locating the artifact, and (b)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m asserts the resulting `.so` is not older than `src/lib.rs` / `Cargo.toml`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     95[0m:[38;5;10m[49m aborting with `STALE ARTIFACT: …` otherwise.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     96[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     97[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The suite's sensitivity was then confirmed by mutation testing — each of these
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m injected defects is caught, so the assertions are not vacuous:
