[38;5;252m[1m## Two things worth your attention[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mA harness bug that made the suite vacuous.[22m [38;5;10mcargo test[0m does not build a [38;5;10mcrate-type = ["cdylib"][0m library — an integration test can't link against a cdylib, so Cargo skips it. My first four green runs were testing a stale [38;5;10m.so[0m from an earlier [38;5;10mcargo build[0m. I caught it by mutation testing: injecting a diagnostic-text typo and an off-by-one bound both "passed." [38;5;10mrust_lib()[0m now shells out to [38;5;10mcargo build --lib[0m with the matching profile/features and aborts on [38;5;10mSTALE ARTIFACT[0m if the [38;5;10m.so[0m predates the sources. After the fix, all five injected defects are caught (table in [38;5;10mSYMBOLS.md[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mOne documented divergence, in C's undefined region.[22m For [38;5;10mbad(data)[0m with [38;5;10mdata >= 12[0m, the C's overrun reaches the saved frame pointer ([38;5;10mdata[0m 12–13) or the return address ([38;5;10mdata >= 14[0m) — disassembly puts [38;5;10mbuffer[0m at [38;5;10m-0x30(%rbp)[0m and [38;5;10mi[0m at [38;5;10m-0x4(%rbp)[0m. Its behavior depends on the [3mcaller's[23m stack, not the library: from the test child, C survives 12, 13, 20, 32, 64, 100, 500, 1000 but takes [38;5;10mSIGSEGV[0m on 14 and 15; from a Python [38;5;10mctypes[0m caller it crashed from 12 onward. No sound Rust can reproduce "corrupt my caller's frame," so [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m row 9 is measured and reported rather than equality-asserted, and the assertion there is that Rust stays deterministic. C and Rust agree byte-for-byte across the entire deterministic domain [38;5;10mINT_MIN..=11[0m, including the benign overruns at 10 and 11.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I made one change to [38;5;10msrc/lib.rs[0m: [38;5;10mbad()[0m derived its out-of-bounds pointer from the 10-element subslice, which is UB in Rust (wrong provenance) even though the backing array is 1024 elements — an optimizer would have been entitled to break it. It now derives from the full backing array and skips writes past the slack region. No observable output changes; verified in both dev and release.[0m[0m
